 "text": "The doctor who told other doctors to wash their hands was rejected. 1847, Vienna. Dr. Ignaz Semmelweis notices something terrible. New mothers treated by doctors die of a fever, far more often than those treated by midwives. The doctors often come straight from doing autopsies, so he orders them to wash their hands in a chlorine solution. Deaths drop sharply. But many doctors refuse to believe they're the problem. Semmelweis dies in 1865, years before germs are widely accepted. Every legend has a beginning.",
